{
  "text": "The conversation piece by Wintermeier argues that the idea of a single emergency switch for AI governance is misleading, as it oversimplifies the complex infrastructure and human decisions involved. In contrast, the scholarly study found that adding self-regulation prompts and emotional support to AI interactions improved students' enjoyment and reduced boredom, but did not significantly enhance knowledge or transfer. Both sources highlight limitations: Wintermeier's commentary is not an empirical evaluation of AI controls, while the study's intervention was brief and its follow-up incomplete.",
