{
  "text": "Both studies explore the impact of AI on self-regulated learning. The first study, involving SRL-based chatbots, found that while all groups improved in knowledge and learning transfer, the differences were not statistically significant. However, the SRL-based chatbots enhanced enjoyment and reduced boredom, and showed better task-level performance and reflection. The second study, using reflective learning dashboards, reported significant improvements in self-regulated learning behaviors, time on task, login frequency, and academic performance. Despite these positive outcomes, both studies have limitations. The first study's intervention was limited to a single 25-minute session, and the knowledge tests had low reliability. The second study, while effective, only lasted 12 weeks and did not fully address long-term effects.",
